      "title": "Note",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# TEST: EPS Prompt Builder - compose from the Notebook (v0.76.0)\n\n**Setup (once):** copy `eps-cross-test-prompts.md` (next to this file in\n`examples/`) into your library folder - the same file the Run Multiplier\ndemo uses. Then press **Run**.\n\nThe Notebook on the left has **Neon City + Golden Hour** selected and is\npiped into the Builder. The Builder's blocks are **Ink Sketch, Pastel\nStudio** - live references to the same file.\n\n## Pass 1 - just Run\n\nTwo \"Preview as Text\" nodes show TWO combined prompts (one per selected\nnotebook entry - the sweep axis passes through):\n\n- `Neon City's text, Ink Sketch's text, Pastel Studio's text`\n- `Golden Hour's text, Ink Sketch's text, Pastel Studio's text`\n\nThe name preview shows `Neon City+Ink Sketch+Pastel Studio` and\n`Golden Hour+Ink Sketch+Pastel Studio`.\n\n## Pass 2 - reorder and delete\n\nDrag `Pastel Studio` above `Ink Sketch` on the Builder's right pane, Run:\nthe combined order flips. Click x on a block: only the block disappears -\nthe Notebook and the md file are untouched.\n\n## Pass 3 - live references\n\nEdit `Ink Sketch`'s text in the NOTEBOOK (not the Builder - the Builder's\nleft list is read-only on purpose), Run: the Builder picks up the new text\nautomatically. Rename an entry the Builder uses and the block turns red\n(\"missing\") and the queue fails naming it - fix by re-adding the renamed\nprompt or deleting the block.\n\n## Pass 4 - alone\n\nDisconnect the Notebook wires: the Builder still runs, emitting ONE\ncombined prompt from its blocks alone.\n"
      ]
    }
